AB  - Research on LLM-based test code generation has achieved significant progress at the function level, yet extending it to the class level introduces new challenges arising from its complex dependencies and shared variables. Existing approaches typically generate all test code at once through prompting, with relatively limited evaluation metrics, making it difficult to effectively address class-level generation tasks. To this end, we introduce a multi-agent collaboration approach for test code generation and introduce scenario count and mutation score metrics as supplementary metrics, building a multi-dimensional and comprehensive evaluation. Based on the ClassEval dataset, we conduct experiments on four China-developed LLMs, totaling 1,200 samples. Experimental results show that the multi-agent approach outperforms existing approaches in overall performance, achieving the best accuracy and comparable coverage, while generating significantly more test scenarios.
ER  - 

